commit 8d11ba0d94bde2473885e2950850d528ab6d3e0b
Author: Samridhi <samridhi@nhai2026.dev>
Date:   Mon Jun 1 20:30:41 2026 +0000

    feat: Challenge-Response Liveness Detection + NHAI Shift Punctuality Engine
    
    Feature 1 — LivenessChallenge.ts (src/services/)
      Anti-spoofing geometric challenge-response system:
      - newChallenge(): picks random direction LEFT | RIGHT | UP
      - evaluateFrame(): computes YAW ratio (nose_x normalised by face width)
        and PITCH ratio (nose_y relative to eye centre) from BlazeFace landmarks
      - ChallengePassed only after HOLD_FRAMES (8) consecutive in-threshold frames
      - fromFaceDetection(): bridges existing TFLiteService output to landmark format
      - Configurable thresholds: YAW_LEFT_MAX=0.35, YAW_RIGHT_MIN=0.65, PITCH_UP_MAX=0.30
      - 10-second timeout with expired flag
      - Demo mode: simulated landmark drift so feature works without real models
    
    Feature 2 — ShiftPunctuality.ts (src/utils/)
      NHAI operational shift punctuality engine:
      - Morning Shift   06:00–14:00, 15-min grace
      - Afternoon Shift 14:00–22:00, 15-min grace
      - Night Shift     22:00–06:00, midnight crossover handled correctly
      - Returns: currentShift, status (ON_TIME|LATE|EARLY), minutesDeviated, message
      - toDBStatus() maps to existing 'Present'|'Late' DB column
      - EARLY_THRESHOLD_MINUTES=60 prevents false early flags near shift boundaries
    
    AttendanceScreen.tsx — integrated both features
      - Phase state machine: IDLE → CHALLENGE → RECOGNISING → DONE
      - Orange oval border pulses during challenge phase
      - Animated progress bar shows liveness completion percentage
      - Direction icon (⬅️ ➡️ ⬆️) + prompt text displayed on camera overlay
      - Recognition only runs after challenge.passed === true
      - Punctuality result shown inline in scan log with colour coding
        (green = On Time, amber = Late)
      - Anti-spoofing info card shown in IDLE state
    
    DatabaseService.ts — fixed duplicate 'designation' field in Employee interface

